(272036, 18165, 3290, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments.<br/> <br/>For all those who asked, these are Cadbury''s Flake bars (actually, the shortened ''99'' version which are for putting in ice cream). Setup was a stack on my kitchen workstop with a single halogen light to the right. I agree with those comments which suggested the light should have been more from the front than it is - I ran out of time.<br/> <br/>Flakes are readily available in the UK. In the US, you can order them from <a href="//www.britishdelights.com/cadbury.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">British Delights</a>. (I have no affiliation with this company and have never used them.)</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments. For all those who asked, these are Cadbury''s Flake bars (actually, the shortened ''99'' version which are for putting in ice cream). Setup was a stack on my kitchen workstop with a single halogen light to the right. I agree with those comments which suggested the light should have been more from the front than it is - I ran out of time. Flakes are readily available in the UK. In the US, you can order them from British Delights. (I have no affiliation with this company and have never used them.)', '2003-04-21 07:19:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(272039, 18029, 3306, '<td valign="top">Wow, 51 comments! Thanks everyone for your remarks. I wish I had more time to work on this one and get the focus better as that seems to be the overriding problem with my picture. I had difficulty getting the proper lighting, finally moving my M&amp;M''s outside but it was too cloudy. The picture didn''t take as many M&amp;M''s as it appears as I used a mirror to give it that appearance. There in lies some of my problem with focus. I agree that it is oversharp. It makes it look like I took a picture of a picture, but that is not the case. Thanks again for everyone''s suggestions.</td>', 'Wow, 51 comments! Thanks everyone for your remarks. I wish I had more time to work on this one and get the focus better as that seems to be the overriding problem with my picture. I had difficulty getting the proper lighting, finally moving my M&M''s outside but it was too cloudy. The picture didn''t take as many M&M''s as it appears as I used a mirror to give it that appearance. There in lies some of my problem with focus. I agree that it is oversharp. It makes it look like I took a picture of a picture, but that is not the case. Thanks again for everyone''s suggestions.', '2003-04-21 07:29:24.000000', NULL, 0),
