(273307, 18031, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Shari...<br/> <br/>I love PEZ :)  This photo does bring back a memory of a unique flavor in my childhood... I had a box full of the dispensers and I sort of ''collected'' them at one point.  The family Friday night dinner at the local fish camp was a treat for me because this is where I found a vending machine that sold the dispensers and candy.  <br/> <br/>Your composition on this photo is quite colorful and well organized.  This composition is definitely worthy of an ''advertisement'' photograph.  The exposure on this seems a little hot, but I believe you mentioned that you are getting a new camera :)  Some of the color saturation is lost due to that problem.  <br/> <br/>Keep up the good work and I look forward to seeing the results of your new cam :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Shari... I love PEZ :)  This photo does bring back a memory of a unique flavor in my childhood... I had a box full of the dispensers and I sort of ''collected'' them at one point.  The family Friday night dinner at the local fish camp was a treat for me because this is where I found a vending machine that sold the dispensers and candy.   Your composition on this photo is quite colorful and well organized.  This composition is definitely worthy of an ''advertisement'' photograph.  The exposure on this seems a little hot, but I believe you mentioned that you are getting a new camera :)  Some of the color saturation is lost due to that problem.   Keep up the good work and I look forward to seeing the results of your new cam :) John Setzler', '2003-04-22 09:13:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(273344, 18031, 7466, '<td valign="top">John,<br/> <br/>Thanks for your comments :).  You''re right, the new camera is on its way as I type.  The problem with the old one was a bad exposure meter (can''t ya tell LOL).</td>', 'John, Thanks for your comments :).  You''re right, the new camera is on its way as I type.  The problem with the old one was a bad exposure meter (can''t ya tell LOL).', '2003-04-22 10:12:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(273349, 17804, 7466, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>I absolutely love the detail and sharp focus achieved in this shot.  The clarity of the features on the gummi bears is amazing.  I also like the colors and lighting.  <br/> <br/>The vibrant colors are great fun and the lighting is bright enough to give the gummi bears a nice glow but not so bright as to set up a glare.<br/> <br/>The overall composition, however, seems to lack something and to be honest, I don''t know that I can put my finger on what it is.  I think maybe it is the deliberate placement of the bears as opposed to a more random arrangement.  Of course, this is just that "gut" kind of reaction I had to the image.  Technically, I think you did a great job.  I think the shot just does not appeal to me aesthetically.<br/> <br/>Shari</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) I absolutely love the detail and sharp focus achieved in this shot.  The clarity of the features on the gummi bears is amazing.  I also like the colors and lighting.   The vibrant colors are great fun and the lighting is bright enough to give the gummi bears a nice glow but not so bright as to set up a glare. The overall composition, however, seems to lack something and to be honest, I don''t know that I can put my finger on what it is.  I think maybe it is the deliberate placement of the bears as opposed to a more random arrangement.  Of course, this is just that "gut" kind of reaction I had to the image.  Technically, I think you did a great job.  I think the shot just does not appeal to me aesthetically. Shari', '2003-04-22 10:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(273598, 18138, 4482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC!<br/> <br/>MEETS THE CHALLENGE: IMO it didn''t meet the challenge even though I love the stuff! :-P But not candy to me.<br/> <br/>LIGHTING &amp; FOCUS: light saturation is good but the yellowish tone draws away from the yummyness of it. A nice WB check would have solved this problem ro reducing the yellow saturation. Focus is good the somewhat shalow DOF isn''t distracting to the eye and works well here.<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION: I like the shot angle an the fact that we see some BG. It brings the focus back to the food. Your frame is clean and simple and not distracting. Good job on that one!<br/> <br/>All in all a good photo. No WOW factor here though.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Yanik</td>', 'Greetings from the CC! MEETS THE CHALLENGE: IMO it didn''t meet the challenge even though I love the stuff! :-P But not candy to me. LIGHTING & FOCUS: light saturation is good but the yellowish tone draws away from the yummyness of it. A nice WB check would have solved this problem ro reducing the yellow saturation. Focus is good the somewhat shalow DOF isn''t distracting to the eye and works well here. COMPOSITION: I like the shot angle an the fact that we see some BG. It brings the focus back to the food. Your frame is clean and simple and not distracting. Good job on that one! All in all a good photo. No WOW factor here though. Keep up the good work! Yanik', '2003-04-22 14:27:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(273621, 18127, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Ayme :)<br/> <br/>Jay looks like a cool turtle :)  He apparently likes candy as much as i do.. lol... The detail of the turtle is excellent and the underside perspective is strong also.  <br/> <br/>As I said in my original comment on this photo, I think the theme of ''candy'' is overshadowed by the turtle itself.  Candy is present in the photo so it does meet the challenge :)<br/> <br/>I like to spend some time evaluating the meaning of each challenge and I don''t usually get on the fringes of what I think the challenge means.  It''s like in the flora competition this week, I see a lot of photos that contain flora, but the flora is overshadowed by some larger and stronger theme in the image... does that make sense?<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Ayme :) Jay looks like a cool turtle :)  He apparently likes candy as much as i do.. lol... The detail of the turtle is excellent and the underside perspective is strong also.   As I said in my original comment on this photo, I think the theme of ''candy'' is overshadowed by the turtle itself.  Candy is present in the photo so it does meet the challenge :) I like to spend some time evaluating the meaning of each challenge and I don''t usually get on the fringes of what I think the challenge means.  It''s like in the flora competition this week, I see a lot of photos that contain flora, but the flora is overshadowed by some larger and stronger theme in the image... does that make sense? Keep up the good work :) John Setzler', '2003-04-22 15:39:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(273627, 17804, 1031, '<td valign="top">Maybe it would have been more "convincing" had you stood them up, like viewing a square dance from obliquely above. We needn''t see all of them face-on.<br/> <br/>Despite your note, I have a suspicion some bears were harmed AFTER the making of this shot...</td>', 'Maybe it would have been more "convincing" had you stood them up, like viewing a square dance from obliquely above. We needn''t see all of them face-on. Despite your note, I have a suspicion some bears were harmed AFTER the making of this shot...', '2003-04-22 15:43:58.000000', NULL, 0),
